 <h2>The mobile app</h2>
 <p>The SG Social Services app for Android and iOS works the same way as this website. Services you save with the star, and your light or dark appearance choice, are kept only on your phone and are never sent to us. The app keeps a copy of the directory on your phone so it works offline. It doesn't use accounts, location, contacts, advertising or tracking.</p>
 
+<h2 id="jobs">The jobs board and jobs assistant</h2>
+<p>Jobs on the board are copied from public listings, mostly MyCareersFuture, and checked every day. Each one links to the original listing, where you apply. We don't take applications, CVs or contact details, and we don't share anything about you with employers.</p>
+<p>What you type into the jobs assistant is sent to Anthropic's Claude model to pick out suitable jobs and write your recommendations. It isn't saved on our side: the conversation lives in your browser tab and is gone when you press "Start over" or close the page. Anthropic doesn't use it to train its models. Please leave out your NRIC, phone number, email and address; the assistant refuses messages that contain them. We only count how many times the jobs assistant was used each day.</p>
+
 <h2>Visit counts</h2>
 <p>To show funders and partners that the directory is used, the site keeps simple daily counts: how many visits and page views there were, how many searches were made, which presenting-issue pages and filters were used, and how many times the assistant was used. That's all. We don't use cookies for this, and we don't store your IP address, device details, the words you search for or anything you type into the assistant. If your browser has Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control switched on, you aren't counted at all.</p>
 <p>We also count roughly how many different people visit, and which country visits come from. For the first, your browser remembers the last date it was counted (for example "19 November 2026") so it isn't counted twice in a day or month; that date stays on your device and only "+1 visitor" is sent to us. For the second, our host, Netlify, works out the country from your connection and we add 1 to that country's count. We never see or store your IP address or anything more precise than the country.</p>
